mvx: log device discovery and client frame-rate negotiation at INFO, not WARNING

Two normal events in the Linlon VPU driver are logged at WARNING, so a healthy
boot and ordinary video playback both report warnings that are not problems.

1. mvx_dev.c — "Linlon vX identified. cores=..." is device discovery. It is
   printed once per probe on every successful boot. That is an INFO-level fact,
   not a warning.

2. mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c — "v4l2: Invalid frame period from client" fires whenever a
   client requests a frame rate the VPU will not convert. The word "Invalid" is
   misleading: the request is well-formed and the driver's own comment says
   "Just do sanity check but not update fps as VPU doesn't support frame rate
   conversion". The code immediately returns the supported rate and continues,
   which is successful negotiation. Chromium requests 1/30 and triggers this on
   every single playback, so a user watching video accumulates kernel warnings
   at the rate they open videos.

Measured on a Radxa Orion O6 (CIX Sky1, cix-vpu-driver 1.0.2, kernel
7.2.0-rc7): with these two lines alone changed, boot-time kernel warnings fell
from 40 to 36 and the "identified" line moved off the warning level entirely
(warn=0, info=0 at default console loglevel). No behaviour changes — only the
severity of two log statements.

UPSTREAM STATUS: to be sent to CIX. This is a vendor DKMS package
(cix-vpu-driver), not an in-tree driver, so it cannot go via lore. Note the
in-tree copy under drivers/media/platform/cix/ carries the same two lines and
was fixed separately in the NCZ kernel tree; on NCZ the in-tree amvx.ko is
deliberately not built, so the DKMS copy is the one that runs and this patch is
the one that matters.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/dev/mvx_dev.c	2026-08-03 21:00:52.000000000 -0400
+++ b/driver/dev/mvx_dev.c	2026-08-10 09:50:19.483401950 -0400
@@ -1051,7 +1051,7 @@
         goto devfreq_remove;
     }
 
-    MVX_LOG_PRINT(&mvx_log_dev, MVX_LOG_WARNING,
+    MVX_LOG_PRINT(&mvx_log_dev, MVX_LOG_INFO,
               "Linlon v%x identified. cores=%u, core_mask=0x%x, nlsid=%u, id=%u.",
               mvx_hwreg_get_hw_id(&ctx->hwreg),
               mvx_hwreg_get_ncores(&ctx->hwreg),
--- a/driver/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c	2026-08-03 21:00:52.000000000 -0400
+++ b/driver/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c	2026-08-10 09:50:19.517613591 -0400
@@ -1484,7 +1484,7 @@
         frameperiod = &a->parm.capture.timeperframe;
         if (frameperiod->numerator * session->fps_n != frameperiod->denominator * session->fps_d ||
             frameperiod->numerator == 0 || frameperiod->denominator == 0) {
-            MVX_SESSION_WARN(&session,
+            MVX_SESSION_INFO(&session,
                 "v4l2: Invalid frame period from client (%d/%d). Return %d/%d",
                 frameperiod->numerator, frameperiod->denominator, session->fps_n, session->fps_d);
             frameperiod->numerator = session->fps_d;
